# ce-default-wallpaper — webOS CE: make the CE wallpaper the out-of-box
# default. Only replaces the factory wallpaper (01.jpg on hp.tar, 02.jpg on
# att.tar, read from customization.json); any user choice is left alone.
# Triggers BOTH per boot and at first-use completion: the OOBE finishes
# without a reboot (markFirstUseDone + LunaSysMgr respawn), so a job that
# only ran on 'stopped finish' fired before first use and then never again
# (seen live: factory wallpaper survived a whole no-reboot flash).
#
# The flag is set ONLY after re-reading the preference and seeing the CE
# wallpaper actually stick. It used to be set unconditionally, outside the
# `if`, with both luna-send replies discarded — so an import that failed
# (or simply had not finished: lsq hard-kills the call after 4s, and the
# customization pass that copies the wallpaper into /media/internal runs
# CONCURRENTLY with this job's first-use-finished run) left the pref
# pointing at a file that was never imported, permanently, with no second
# boot to repair it. Also wait for the source file to exist before trying.
# Third trigger: `started LunaSysMgr` — the first-use-finished emit is
# fire-and-forget from a process calling exit(0), so it can be lost.

start on stopped finish
start on first-use-finished
start on started LunaSysMgr

console none

script
    exec sh -e /usr/palm/ce-seed/jobs/ce-default-wallpaper.sh
end script
